cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it along with the underlying tools (see 'references')."
title: "ADME-Lab: Analog Design, Synthetic Reactions and Self-Verified ADME/Tox & IUPAC Prediction"
abstract: >-
  An open cheminformatics toolkit to design and enumerate molecules (R-group
  decoration, BRICS, and an extensible synthetic-reaction engine), predict their
  ADME properties and acute toxicity (LD50), assign self-verified IUPAC names via
  an OPSIN round-trip, and rank/select candidates. Reaction types are pluggable
  (esterification and amidation included).
